          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">01</span>What does Seascape charge to manage a vacation rental?</summary>
          <p>{% include "partials/owner-fee-statement.njk" %}</p>
          <p><a class="g-inline-link" href="#owner-cta" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="property-management" data-placement="fee-answer">Request your 48-hour revenue review</a></p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">02</span>How do I know if my market can support professional management fees?</summary>
          <p>Start with the services and fee basis in the agreement, then compare it with Seascape's fee of 17–20% of net rent. Read the <a href="/research/owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026/">Airbnb host fee and card-processing guide</a>, then request a revenue review if you need a property-specific management quote.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">03</span>What should a local manager handle that a remote manager usually misses?</summary>
          <p>The short answer is local response time. Cleaning quality control, maintenance triage, guest screening, and property checks are all weaker when the manager is not operating in-market. The market-specific service pages break down how that changes between <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-bradenton/">Bradenton</a>, <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-sarasota/">Sarasota</a>, and <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-anna-maria-island/">Anna Maria Island</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">04</span>What should I read before choosing a vacation rental manager?</summary>
          <p>Start with the page that matches your market, then read the <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-fees-florida/">fee reality page</a>, the <a href="/property-management/maximize-vacation-rental-income-florida/">income breakdown</a>, and the <a href="/property-management/switch-vacation-rental-management-company/">switch-management page</a> if you think the current setup is the real problem.</p>
        </details>
        <details id="local-management-alternative">
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">05</span>Is Seascape a local alternative to Vacasa or Evolve?</summary>
          <p>Seascape Vacations is an owner-operated vacation rental manager for pool homes in Bradenton and Sarasota. Sawyer and Patrick are the people you reach about your home. The team handles listings on Airbnb, Vrbo and its direct-booking site, pricing, guest care, cleaning and maintenance coordination. Your management fee is quoted for your property as a share of net rent after a review, with the basis, included services and separate charges in writing.</p>
          <p><a class="g-inline-link" href="#owner-cta" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="property-management" data-placement="local-alternative">Request your 48-hour revenue review</a></p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">06</span>What does full-service management from Seascape include?</summary>
          <p>Seascape's full-service management covers the same five jobs for every home we manage: listing it on Airbnb, Vrbo and our own booking site; setting and adjusting nightly rates as demand moves; screening and messaging guests from Bradenton; coordinating cleaning and maintenance, with a note before you have to ask; and paying you monthly with a statement of what your home earned and spent, with county taxes remitted.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">07</span>What should I ask any vacation rental manager before comparing fees?</summary>
          <p>Ask what the percentage is taken from, gross or net rent, and what is billed separately, such as setup, maintenance or card processing. Then ask who answers guests and handles problems locally, how nightly rates are set, and what your monthly statement and payout show. Seascape quotes each home individually and puts those answers in writing after a review.</p>
        </details>
